# Element read keeps its subtype for later arithmetic

Verifies `let first = sizes[0]` keeps the stored millimeter subtype, so
`first + 1mm` uses the normal measure arithmetic and yields 11mm.

>>> source
let sizes: int[] = [10mm, 2cm]
let first = sizes[0]
print(first)
print(first + 1mm)

<<< stdout
10mm
11mm

<<< stderr
